This ruling batch covers all eight action IDs across four actors in three integrated rulings. R1 adjudicates Starbucks' pilot launch and instrumentation as a structural setup (no measured outcomes, all observed fields preserved null). R2 adjudicates the three buyer personas jointly, recognizing their trigger conditions are contingent on an unresolved branch (slot displacement rate), and plays the moderate_displacement branch as the adjudicated outcome. R3 integrates all five Dutch Bros and Dunkin actions as a single competitor-response ruling, tracing the shared demand-source dependency, confirming budget feasibility, and recording simulated estimates in separately named fields distinct from null observed fields. All causal links declare their basis explicitly; no invented observations are presented as measurements; kill criteria are listed but all remain unevaluated because evidence fields are null at move-one close.

